```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: Periodic Beaconing Pattern to External Host
# Detection ID: DE-C2-001
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1071.001 - Application Layer Protocol: Web Protocols / T1132 - Data Encoding
# Data Source: Proxy/firewall logs (sourcetype=proxy)
# Severity: High
# ============================================================================

index=network sourcetype=proxy
| bucket _time span=1h
| stats count values(uri_path) as paths by src_ip, dest, _time
| streamstats current=f window=2 last(_time) as prev_time by src_ip, dest
| eventstats stdev(count) as stdev_count avg(count) as avg_count by src_ip, dest
| eval coefficient_of_variation=round(stdev_count/avg_count,3)
| where coefficient_of_variation<0.15 AND avg_count>=10
| dedup src_ip, dest
| table src_ip, dest, avg_count, coefficient_of_variation, paths
```

## Detection Logic
C2 frameworks (Cobalt Strike, Sliver, custom implants) beacon at regular intervals with jitter. Low coefficient-of-variation in hourly connection counts to the same destination over time is a strong statistical signature of automated beaconing versus organic human browsing traffic.

## False Positive Considerations
SaaS health-check/heartbeat integrations (monitoring agents, license checks) beacon similarly — maintain an allowlist of known SaaS telemetry endpoints; also tune window length to reduce noise from short observation periods.

## Tuning Notes
Requires at least 72 hours of proxy log retention in the search window to compute a statistically meaningful coefficient of variation; this is a hunting-oriented search best run daily/weekly rather than real-time.
